# Test: `show config dump -` reads the configuration from stdin.
#
# VALIDATES: the "-" token reaches the config path of the DATA spelling of the
#            dump command, so an operator can pipe a configuration into it and
#            render the answer with any format operator.
# PREVENTS: the argument scan reading "-" as an option and dropping it with the
#           flags. dataDump (internal/component/config/cli/config_data.go) tested
#           only for a leading dash, so `show config dump -` answered
#           "error: missing config file (use - for stdin)" and exited 1, while
#           `ze config dump -` beside it worked. The four .ci cases that used
#           this command to read a config back were red for that reason, and
#           docs/architecture/testing/ci-format.md recommends the same command as
#           the readback for strengthening an accept-only test.
#
# The "-" sits INSIDE the `-c` value rather than in its own argv slot, so the
# runner's "-" to temp-file rewrite (internal/test/runner/parsing.go) does not
# see it: the payload reaches the process on the real stdin fd.
#
# test/ui/dash-stdio.ci covers the `ze config <sub> -` PRINTER half of the same
# pair. This case cannot live beside it: the ui suite splits an exec line with
# strings.Fields, so the quotes around a `ze cli -c "..."` value survive into the
# argv (plan/journal/delegation-hands-the-callee-a-different-argv.md, 2026-08-31).

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	router-id 1.2.3.4
	session {
		asn {
			local 65000
		}
	}
	peer edge1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 1.1.1.1
			}
			local {
				ip 2.2.2.2
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				remote 65001
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze cli -c "show config dump - | json":stdin=config
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:pattern="router-id": "1.2.3.4"
expect=stdout:pattern="remote": "65001"

# The same read with the strip-private flag beside it: the flag is recognized and
# the "-" is still the path, so one does not consume the other.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze cli -c "show config dump --strip-private - | json":stdin=config
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:pattern="router-id": "1.2.3.4"
